abstract: >-
  LaTeX source, figures, check program and Lean 4 file of the paper
  "Weak-Type Endpoint Bounds for Bochner-Riesz Means in Every Dimension".
  At the critical index the Bochner-Riesz means in every dimension n >= 2 are
  of weak type (p,p) for 1 < p < 2n/(n+1), uniformly in the radius, with
  convergence in weak L^p; they have sparse bounds that are sharp on the
  critical side except at one corner, and weighted weak-type bounds for A_1
  weights with a range of p governed by the reverse Hoelder exponent and
  including its right end point. The proof reproduces, with credit,
  OpenAI's proof of the local smoothing conjecture (25 October 2026) and the
  epsilon-removal of Beltran, Roos and Seeger.
keywords:
  - Bochner-Riesz means
  - weak-type endpoint
  - sparse domination
  - local smoothing
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23709183"
